# ── What this file is doing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is public. It tracks the SITE SOURCES only: the Quarto pages, the
# reveal.js decks, the standalone interactives, the vendored field tool, and the
# four gold-reference Pybricks programs the cheat sheet links.
#
# Everything coach-side stays out: the planning documents, the decision log, the
# Skills Check machinery, the student photos and results, the route/sim tooling.
# Two of those (docs/, robots_images/) hold children's names, faces and marks —
# the rules below are what stops a stray `git add .` from publishing them.
# Read README.md § "What is not here" before loosening anything.

# ── Build output and tooling noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
/.quarto/
output/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
__pycache__/
.venv/
# jsdom, installed ad-hoc for tools/audit-recap.js (there is no package.json)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# ── Agent configuration — local, and not everyone's ───────────────────────────
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/
/.agents/

# ── Coach-only: planning, student data, the exam ──────────────────────────────
# docs/ carries the bootcamp plan, the decision log, the WRO rules PDF, the deck
# assets, and docs/exam/ — which holds the answer key, the per-student marks and
# both generated exam pages.
docs/
robots_images/

# Belt and braces for the exam pages, wherever they are generated. exam.html
# once published from the repo root carrying the live /exec URL, the exam secret
# and the students' first names. Neither page may be tracked or listed under
# `resources:` in _quarto.yml. See docs/exam/web/README.md.
exam.html
coach.html

# Scraped text of WRO's copyrighted rules PDF; the README links WRO's own
# download page instead.
/extracted_rules_text.txt

# ── Coach tooling stays out — except the field tool the site ships ────────────
# `tools/` cannot be punctured once excluded as a directory, so exclude its
# entries and re-include the one folder. tools/robot_sim/ (the Brython bench)
# and tools/route_optimizer/ are deliberately not distributed.
tools/*
!tools/odommap/

# ── Gold-reference programs: the ones the site links, nothing else ──────────
# library-cheatsheet.qmd declares the first three under `resources:` and offers
# them as downloads; programming-the-claw.qmd does the same for claw_starter.py
# and claw_gripper.py. Without them those links 404. code/.venv/ and
# code/archive/ stay out.
code/*
!code/movements.py
!code/claw_gripper.py
!code/lift_gripper.py
!code/claw_starter.py
